{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q31","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.1","block_identifier":"knowledge-check","question_identifier":"q31","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Call sheet requires show blacks and an early load-in with overhead work. Correct answer: bring the separate clothing/PPE needed for both phases rather than treating show blacks as load-in PPE.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored question normalized; exact PPE remains task/site controlled."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q31","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"3","lesson_identifier":"3.1","block_identifier":"knowledge-check-coaching","question_identifier":"q31","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Show clothing and hazard-selected work PPE can be separate requirements. Preparation means following the call/site requirements for each phase rather than substituting one for the other.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from show-blacks and contextual-PPE claims."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q61","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.1","block_identifier":"knowledge-check","question_identifier":"q61","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"A lead gives an instruction you only partly understand. Correct answer: briefly clarify or restate what you heard rather than claiming understanding or guessing.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Exact sample words are not the assessed competency; confirmation/clarification is."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q61","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-COM","D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"5","lesson_identifier":"5.1","block_identifier":"knowledge-check-coaching","question_identifier":"q61","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Clarification prevents an unverified assumption from becoming a work error. The current production's communication protocol controls the exact phrase used.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from qualified communication claim."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q23","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"2","lesson_identifier":"2.3","block_identifier":"knowledge-check","question_identifier":"q23","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Under schedule or fatigue pressure, correct behavior is to preserve control and communicate the problem rather than hide confusion or take a shortcut.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing scored scenario normalized."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q23","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"2","lesson_identifier":"2.3","block_identifier":"knowledge-check-coaching","question_identifier":"q23","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Pressure and fatigue do not remove the need for controlled behavior. Crew Blueprint teaches reporting loss of control or attention through the current work process rather than hiding it.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"awareness_only","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Underlying fatigue claim retains employer/CBA/break-process qualification."}
{"content_id":"Q-SHF-FUND-Q92","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"question","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.2","block_identifier":"knowledge-check","question_identifier":"q92","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"During load-out, fatigue is causing small errors. Correct answer: do not knowingly mis-pack gear or hide the problem; preserve the assignment standard and communicate through the lead/work process.","content_classification":"assessment_prompt","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Existing fatigue/inventory scenario normalized without claiming a universal break entitlement or load-out risk ranking."}
{"content_id":"QR-SHF-FUND-Q92","domain_id_primary":"D-SHF","domain_ids_secondary":["D-EVD"],"content_type":"answer_rationale","route_file":"courses/stagehand-fundamentals.html","source_data_file":null,"course_id":"C-SHF-FUNDAMENTALS","tier_learning":"T1","responsibility_band":"R0","authority_class":"A0","module_identifier":"8","lesson_identifier":"8.2","block_identifier":"knowledge-check-coaching","question_identifier":"q92","visual_identifier":null,"learner_facing_text":"Fatigue can increase error risk; knowingly using the wrong destination or hiding a deteriorating condition is not a valid shortcut. Report and continue under the controlling work/break process.","content_classification":"source_backed_instruction","safety_criticality":"moderate","authority_implication":"assigned_support","publication_state":"live","supersedes_content_id":null,"superseded_by_content_id":null,"last_content_reviewed_at":"2026-08-31","notes":"Derived from qualified fatigue/pressure claim."}
